A hidden test instance (ARDIA_BACKGROUND=1) never makes itself a system default: shell_integration's
SetAsDefaultBrowser, SetAsDefaultClientForScheme and SetAsDefaultHandlerForUTType log a line and return false. Every
Chrome path goes through them (chrome://settings' Make default, the default browser prompt, a protocol handler made
default), so an agent's click in a scratch copy can't change the owner's default browser, mail client or PDF reader,
and SetAsDefaultBrowser no longer activates CoreServicesUIAgent over the owner's work.

--- a/chrome/browser/shell_integration_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/shell_integration_mac.mm
@@ -6,11 +6,14 @@
 
 #include <AppKit/AppKit.h>
 #include <UniformTypeIdentifiers/UniformTypeIdentifiers.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
